# CMS22 Blood Pressure Screening — measure caseload

// A clinical scenario where a patient at a routine annual wellness visit
// has their blood pressure measured and the reading is normal. The
// patient satisfies the CMS22 Numerator via the Normal BP Reading path.

library "CMS22 Blood Pressure Screening".
covers "cms22".


// ============ Patient facts ============

fact "Maria Garcia":
- name is "Maria Garcia".
- birth date is "1972-08-22".
- defined by "Patient".


// ============ Clinical facts ============

fact "Annual Wellness Visit":
- code is "http://hl7.org/fhir/sid/hcpcs|G0438".
- date is "2026-03-10".
- defined by "cms22-RecordSource"."BP Screening Encounters".

fact "Normal BP Panel":
- code is "http://loinc.org|85354-9".
- date is "2026-03-10".
- defined by "cms22-RecordSource"."Blood Pressure Panels".

fact "Normal Systolic Component":
- code is "http://loinc.org|8480-6".
- date is "2026-03-10".
- value is 118.
- defined by "cms22-RecordSource"."Systolic Blood Pressure Code".

fact "Normal Diastolic Component":
- code is "http://loinc.org|8462-4".
- date is "2026-03-10".
- value is 76.
- defined by "cms22-RecordSource"."Diastolic Blood Pressure Code".


// ============ Cases ============

case "Maria has normal BP at her wellness visit":
- description is `Maria's systolic (118) and diastolic (76) readings on her
  qualifying-encounter day are both below the Normal-BP thresholds, so the
  clinical intent is a Normal BP Reading numerator hit. But CEL cannot yet model
  an Observation's systolic/diastolic as components nested inside the 85354-9 BP
  panel (a fact-model gap tracked in #285); the readings can only be authored as
  standalone Observations. The emitted Normal BP Reading reads the systolic and
  diastolic as a component of the panel, which is empty for this data, so every
  Numerator path evaluates false and the Numerator is false here. This asserts the
  hand-traced determination, not the clinical intent; result-is execution is also
  deferred (#70).`.
- subject is "Maria Garcia".
- fact is "Annual Wellness Visit".
- fact is "Normal BP Panel".
- fact is "Normal Systolic Component".
- fact is "Normal Diastolic Component".
- result is "Initial Population" is true.
- result is "Numerator" is false.
